15d49b2a90"},{"path":"src/tracker/index.js","sha256":"e666bf6893e4eb58677d57199d665fa3d47f84a70684d3aa148a715a455fd14b"}],"queries":[{"id":"repoqa-802eb3db0854463c9162","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to generate a concatenated key name based on a current key and its parent key, primarily used in hierarchical data structures.\n2. **Input**: Takes two strings: the current key and the parent key.\n3. **Output**: Returns a single string that represents the full path of the key, combining the parent key and the current key with a dot if a parent key exists.\n4. **Procedure**: Checks if a parent key is provided. If not, it returns the current key as is. If a parent key exists, it concatenates the parent key with the current key using a dot as a separator and returns the resulting string.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/lib/data.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[84,90]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-66db7fd9d58b3b3c49c4","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to transform an array of filter objects into a single object where each key corresponds to the name of a filter, facilitating easier access and manipulation of filter data.\n2. **Input**: The function accepts an array of objects, where each object contains properties such as `name`, `type`, `operator`, and `value`.\n3. **Output**: It returns an object where each key is the `name` from the filter objects in the input array, and the value is the corresponding filter object.\n4. **Procedure**: The function iterates over the input array, using the `reduce` method to accumulate the results into a single object. For each filter in the array, it adds a new property to the accumulator object using the filter's `name` as the key and the filter object itself as the value.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/pages/api/reports/insights.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[58,64]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-fec9a5ad31450b682491","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To verify if a user has reached a usage limit and block further actions if they have.\n2. **Input**: A unique identifier for a user.\n3. **Output**: Throws an error if the user is blocked due to reaching the usage limit; otherwise, no output.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first checks if the blocking feature is enabled. If it is, it queries a cache to see if the user is already blocked. If the user is blocked, it increments the block count for monitoring purposes and throws an error indicating that the usage limit has been reached.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/lib/session.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[123,129]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-1500a6bb924e68086e03","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to retrieve retention data for a specific website over a given time period, using different database technologies based on configuration.\n2. **Input**: The function accepts a tuple containing a string identifier for the website and a filters object specifying start and end dates, with an optional timezone.\n3. **Output**: The function returns retention data, the specifics of which depend on the underlying database query results.\n4. **Procedure**: The function determines which database technology to use (relational or ClickHouse) based on configuration. It then executes a corresponding query function with the provided parameters to fetch retention data from the selected database.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/queries/analytics/reports/getRetention.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[5,19]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-1bc7937d574d24bb7e3c","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function determines which time units are appropriate for use based on the difference between two provided dates.\n2. **Input**: Two date objects representing the start and end dates.\n3. **Output**: An array of strings, each representing a time unit that is suitable given the span between the two dates.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first identifies the smallest relevant time unit for the given date range. It then filters out finer units that are not suitable for representing the span between the two dates, returning only those units that are appropriate.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/lib/date.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[251,257]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-7e568991bc551396a224","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To gather and return various statistical metrics related to the performance and user engagement of a specific website over a given time period.\n2. **Input**: A unique identifier for the website and a set of filtering criteria which includes date ranges and other parameters relevant to the website's events.\n3. **Output**: A collection of statistics such as page views, unique visitors, total visits, bounce rates, and total engagement time.\n4. **Procedure**: The function selects the appropriate database query method based on the environment (relational or ClickHouse). It then executes a complex SQL query that filters website events within the specified date range and calculates different engagement metrics. The results are formatted and returned as structured data.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/queries/analytics/getWebsiteStats.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[7,16]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-2c1ded4ecaa2813cb459","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: To provide a list of language names based on the specified locale, ensuring the data is up-to-date by fetching it from a server if not already cached.\n2. **Input**: A string representing the locale (e.g., 'en-US').\n3. **Output**: A list of language names appropriate to the given locale.\n4. **Procedure**: \n   - Initially, the function checks if the language data for the specified locale is already available in a local cache.\n   - If the data is not in the cache, it fetches the data asynchronously from a server using a specified endpoint and updates the cache.\n   - The function then sets the fetched or cached data as the state, which is returned to the component that invoked this function.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/components/hooks/useLanguageNames.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[9,32]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-25dd5dcb184ca21937eb","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to analyze user interactions on a website by tracking the progression through specified steps within a given timeframe, helping to understand user behavior and conversion rates.\n2. **Input**: It accepts a unique identifier for the website, a set of criteria including the time window in minutes, start and end dates, and a sequence of steps each defined by a type and a value.\n3. **Output**: The function returns a list of steps with statistics for each step, including the number of visitors who reached that step, the number who dropped off from the previous step, the drop-off rate, and the percentage of visitors remaining from the initial count.\n4. **Procedure**: The function determines which database to query based on configuration, executes a query to fetch data for each step within the specified timeframe, and then processes the results to calculate the metrics for each step, such as visitor counts and drop-off rates.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/queries/analytics/reports/getFunnel.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[24,39]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-c31bfc4fd8a9c8d99e8a","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function is designed to modify the details of an existing team entity in the database.\n2. **Input**: It accepts a unique identifier for the team and a set of new values to update in the team's record.\n3. **Output**: Returns the updated team entity after applying the changes.\n4. **Procedure**: The function first specifies the team to be updated using its unique identifier. It then applies the provided updates along with the current timestamp to mark when the update occurred. Finally, it commits these changes to the database and returns the updated team entity.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/queries/admin/team.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[102,114]]}],"answerability":"answerable"},{"id":"repoqa-f30b8dcf83678f876174","text":"\n1. **Purpose**: The function calculates the difference in seconds between two timestamp fields.\n2. **Input**: Two timestamp fields (start and end).\n3. **Output**: A string representing a SQL query that when executed, returns the difference in seconds between the two timestamps.\n4. **Procedure**: Depending on the database type (either PostgreSQL or MySQL), the function constructs a SQL query using database-specific functions to calculate the difference in seconds between the two provided timestamp fields.\n","group":"umami-software/umami","split":"test","workload":"code-agent","kind":"function-description","gold":[{"path":"src/lib/prisma.ts","grade":2,"spans":[[84,94]]}],"answerability":"answerable"}]}
